    {
      "filename": "Another sight from Yokohama's Chinatown (4611773858).jpg",
      "title": "File:Another sight from Yokohama's Chinatown (4611773858).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e2/Another_sight_from_Yokohama%27s_Chinatown_%284611773858%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Another_sight_from_Yokohama%27s_Chinatown_(4611773858).jpg",
      "width": 2592,
      "height": 1944,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Jorge Láscar from Australia",
      "description": "Yokohama Chinatown is located on Yokohama, Japan. Just south of Tokyo. It has about 150 years of history. These days only a few Chinese people still live in Chinatown, but it has population of about 3000 to 4000. Most of the residents are from Guangzhou (Canton) but many come from other regions. Yokohama Chinatown is the largest Chinatown in Japan (larger than Chinatowns in both Kobe and Nagasaki) and it is one of the largest in the world. There are over 200 restaurants alone (other shops are not included for this number) [Wikipedia.org]",
      "dateCreated": "2007-01-14 14:54",
